title: Authorizations › Worklist › Updated for a payer change
route: /authorizations
intro: When Payers updates open drafts after a rule change or saved edits, the rows of the cases it redrafted carry a small note 'Updated for a payer change' with the date, under the patient. The note shows the latest update for the case. Rows that no update lists carry no note.
dir: TD
also: Only drafts not sent yet are redrafted; a request the payer already has is never rewritten. Reset demo data clears the notes. The Payers toast and the 'Drafts updated' notification still say Case Manager; the notification opens plain /authorizations, which brings back the last view used.
---
start s1 "Payers › History & Changes: a change is acknowledged and 'Update drafts' is confirmed"
start s0 "Payers › Edits waiting: 'Update drafts' after saved edits"
store st1 "Payers records the update\nWhich change, which payer, the IDs of the drafts and the demo-clock time"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › History & Changes › Review and apply a change"
goto g0 "Continues in: Payers › Edits waiting › Update drafts"
process pd "A redrafted request that is on the Dashboard waits for a new signature\nIt needs you again, so its row counts in 'Needs attention'"
toast nt "Notification 'Drafts updated'\n'2 drafts were redrafted after Cardinal's change. Each needs a new signature in Case Manager.'"
click cn "Click the notification"
process pn "Go to /authorizations (the last view and filters come back)"
start s2 "Open Authorizations"
decision d1 "Does an update list one of the row's IDs?\n(request, case, ledger or draft ID, any letter case)"
process p1 "The newest update for the case is used"
screen t1 "Grey note under the patient\n'Updated for a payer change · 10/20'\nOn a queue request's row, a saved draft's row or a tracked row"
process n1 "No note"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › In progress › Drafts being prepared"
end e1 "Rows are marked"
end e2 "Rows as before"

s1 --> st1 --> g1
s0 --> st1
s0 -.-> g0
st1 --> pd
st1 --> nt --> cn --> pn --> d1
s2 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p1 --> t1 --> e1
t1 -.-> g2
d1 -->|No| n1 --> e2
